Only table names and application components were taken from that file.
Application components of tables not in that file were assigned by this
project and are marked as such (componentInferred).

Field names, key flags and data types were checked once against the
public ECC 6.0 dictionary reference at leanx.eu. Only those technical
facts were used; field labels are original writing for this project.
That site is not consulted automatically again, and the fields are
still to be verified against a real SAP system.
Titles, explanations and synonyms in content/tables/ are original writing
for this project and are not SAP's official descriptions.

The table names, short descriptions, categories and delivery classes in
content/sap-tables.tsv were read once, on 26 October 2026, from the public
table index of SAP Datasheet (https://www.sapdatasheet.org/abap/tabl/),
which reflects the SAP ERP dictionary; its robots.txt allows those pages.
The fields of those tables in content/sap-fields.tsv (name, key flag,
type, short description and check table) were read once, the same day,
from each table's page on SAP Datasheet. The short descriptions are SAP's
own texts, shown in English as SAP wrote them. Each such table links to
its page on SAP Datasheet. See
docs/tablas-sap.md for which tables were included and why.

